#! `$/cancelRequest` reaches the QUERY, not just the transport — the tower-lsp
#! failure report 09 names. Two things make this deterministic rather than a
#! coin flip that passes on slow machines and fails on fast ones:
#!
#!   * the compiler's own injected-slow-query knob, so the query is still
#!     running when the cancel lands;
#!   * `documentSymbol` rather than `hover` as the victim. `hover` goes through
#!     the package-analysis cache, which the `didOpen` publish has already
#!     filled, so it can answer without ever reaching a checkpoint;
#!     `documentSymbol` parses from the snapshot every time and always does.
#!
#! The claims: the cancelled request answers -32800 RequestCancelled — an
#! ANSWER, not silence, because every cancelled request still gets a response —
#! and the session is not poisoned, which the hover afterwards proves.
name      cancel/cancel-inflight
profile   minimal
env       WOLF_QUERY_TEST_SLOW_MS 1500

initialize
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
send      documentSymbol hello.lu
cancel    2
wait      response 2
req       hover hello.lu 8:4
shutdown
